# Vital Relay

Vital Relay is an agentic emergency-response coordination demo built around
Apple health inputs, an authoritative safety boundary, nearby responder
coordination, fixed first-aid protocols, sandboxed local agents, and a bounded
AlphaEvolve-style policy laboratory.

## Current implementation slices

Slices 01 through 11C plus the Wave 2 product foundations are now present:

- **Slice 01:** normalized scalar metric ingestion;
- **Slice 02:** capability ingestion and immutable health snapshots;
- **Slice 03:** scoped PostgreSQL persistence and retention;
- **Slice 04:** authenticated, durable incident ingestion and verification;
- **Slice 05:** PostGIS responder/AED discovery and durable dispatch;
- **Slice 06:** fixed, versioned, source-visible first-aid presentation.
- **Slice 07:** one native app with isolated community, responder, and command
  feature graphs over the real authenticated APIs.
- **Slice 08:** allowlisted APNs registration, durable invitation delivery, and
  an incident-bound native responder handoff.
- **Slice 09:** idempotent command close/handoff, atomic incident resolution and
  assignment revocation, plus native responder exact-data teardown.
- **Slice 10:** durable authenticated persona sessions, secure native
  enrollment/restore, and role-scoped active-incident discovery.
- **Slice 11A:** real foreground Core Location acquisition for deliberate
  authenticated manual SOS.
- **Slice 11B:** real foreground read-only HealthKit scalar ingestion, honest
  capabilities, and immutable context snapshots.
- **Slice 11C:** real `CMFallDetectionManager` callbacks, durable critical-event
  transfer, bounded background iPhone location, and authenticated fall ingestion.
- **Apple Watch foundation:** an embedded watchOS target, typed
  WatchConnectivity envelopes, durable critical-event delivery, coalesced
  telemetry, and honest readiness without synthetic producers.
- **Apple Watch live health:** a user-started `HKWorkoutSession` plus bounded
  pedometer features that start independently, latest-only telemetry, and
  community-session-only iPhone ingestion. Health data remains
  non-authoritative context.
- **ROUTE-01:** real Mapbox-compatible walking directions with bounded parsing,
  durable source-labelled geometry, and an explicit static venue fallback.
- **Agent A2:** a pinned coordination policy, short-lived state-bound tool
  capabilities, five privacy-bounded application tools, and a deny-by-default
  host proxy contract.
- **Agent A3/A3.1:** command-authenticated durable runs, leased PostgreSQL
  control state, real operator-selected NemoClaw or Docker execution,
  authenticated internal HTTP tools, append-only audits, and durable mutation
  idempotency. A runtime failure never invokes the other sandbox.
- **ACE-00:** immutable, content-addressed operational-playbook, delta,
  provenance, role/model identity, and bounded context-selection contracts plus
  a reviewed baseline playbook.
- **ACE Wave 2:** deterministic host merge/storage, redacted offline
  Reflector/Curator clients, verified complete candidate bundles, and mandatory
  reviewed Generator context across live, sandbox, recorded, and scenario runs.
- **WT-60:** an offline AlphaEvolve-style protected evaluation, mutation,
  signed-evidence, archive, promotion, and inherited-improver foundation.
- **Evolution scenario catalog:** 12 development, 6 opaque protected, and 4
  cadence-gated final cases with host-recomputed scoring and signed evidence
  under the accepted trusted-offline-host boundary.

The native app also includes:

- **iOS UI-01:** OLED-dark Living Relay monitoring, replay labeling, animated
  particle heart, deterministic safety check, and bounded response intents.
- **iOS UI-02:** frozen incident Codable parity, authenticated live incident
  transport, durable exact retries, server-owned expiry, polling, Getting Help,
  and Resolved scenes.
- **iOS UI-03:** device-authenticated, privacy-redacted dispatch coordination,
  independent dispatch polling, and a searching/recorded/accepted relay
  constellation with public AED context.
- **Native persona UI:** command state/timeline/coordination/protocol plus a
  responder-token invitation, accept/decline, accepted-only MapKit route, and
  fixed protocol in the same app target. Command can now confirm close or
  external handoff; responder exact data is removed when assignment access ends.
- **Authenticated access UI:** the normal launch restores or enrolls one
  community, responder, or command session, discovers only that role's active
  incidents, and composes a new credential-scoped graph after selection.

Together they provide:

- frozen JSON contracts for `HealthMetric`, `HealthMetricBatch`, and the result;
- a FastAPI `POST /v1/health/metrics:batch` endpoint;
- atomic batch validation and immutable metric IDs;
- idempotent retries and explicit ID-collision responses;
- interchangeable thread-safe in-memory and durable PostgreSQL repositories;
- capability states that never infer HealthKit read denial;
- deterministic live/recent/historical/unavailable display freshness;
- immutable snapshots and a redacted HTTP read model;
- exact retry results across process restarts;
- transactional snapshot capture, explicit demo scopes, and protected retention;
- database-enforced audit immutability and recursive snapshot safety checks;
- database-backed readiness plus bounded PostgreSQL connection waits;
- frozen contracts for real Apple fall callbacks and first-party manual SOS;
- a deterministic incident state machine with durable check-in deadlines;
- atomic event, incident, transition, timeline, health-snapshot, and hold writes;
- idempotent event/check-in receipts and restart-safe timeout processing;
- indexed PostGIS discovery for fresh, available, first-aid-qualified responders;
- nearest-active-AED selection and one-at-a-time durable invitations;
- idempotent authenticated responder decline and acceptance;
- exact wearer-location release only to the accepted responder;
- a persisted responder-to-AED-to-wearer route that uses bounded live walking
  directions when configured and truthfully labels every static fallback;
- deterministic `IncidentKind`-only selection of two fixed protocol versions;
- independently pinned raw-content SHA-256 verification at startup, selection,
  and presentation;
- an append-only protocol snapshot committed with the accepted assignment;
- authenticated command and active assigned-responder protocol reads;
- a responder-authenticated, pre-accept read containing only that responder's
  coarse invitation and current incident version;
- a privacy-bounded responder decision receipt that cannot serialize command
  coordination or another responder profile;
- native command polling for state/version, dispatch, AED, protocol, and the
  ordered timeline;
- native responder accept/decline with durable decision retry, followed by an
  accepted-only MapKit static route and verbatim fixed protocol;
- one iOS composition root for community, responder, and command access profiles
  without mixing persona credentials or accepted-only state;
- responder-authenticated APNs registration with encrypted-at-rest device tokens
  and an explicit seeded-responder allowlist;
- one durable logical notification per invitation, a leased outbox, bounded
  provider receipts, and no retry after an ambiguous provider outcome;
- a privacy-minimal APNs alert whose custom payload contains only schema, kind,
  incident, and invitation identifiers;
- a device-bound Keychain responder profile and notification/deep-link handoff
  that reopens the exact invitation without treating the payload as authority;
- a strict idempotent `close`/`handoff` command whose one PostgreSQL transaction
  resolves the incident and appends its transition, timeline, exact receipt,
  and accepted-assignment revocation;
- retained command incident/timeline/protocol audit with privacy-preserving
  responder denial after revocation;
- native command resolution confirmation and native responder revalidation that
  immediately tears down cached exact location, route, and protocol data;
- operator-provisioned persona accounts with one-way enrollment-token storage;
- installation-bound access/refresh sessions with hashed-only server storage,
  rotation, revocation, and device-only Keychain persistence;
- privacy-minimal active-incident discovery scoped independently to community
  ownership, responder invitations/assignments, or the command demo scope;
- an authenticated-session iPhone launch by default, with fixture and raw-token
  launch arguments retained only as explicit QA paths;
- a real embedded Watch app and restart-safe WatchConnectivity transport that
  keeps critical events separate from latest-only telemetry;
- visible Watch fall authorization plus live-health Start/Stop controls that own
  real fall-detection, HealthKit workout, and pedometer producers;
- a two-phase Apple-fall handoff that persists backend acceptance before Watch
  acknowledgement and never escalates dismissed or rejected callbacks;
- a persona-scoped iPhone telemetry consumer that is destroyed on session
  teardown without touching the fall-critical inbox or retry scheduler;
- manual SOS mapped directly to server escalation and fall verification kept
  backend-authoritative;
- a wearer-safe dispatch client that exposes no accepted route, exact
  coordinate, ETA, or responder credential;
- Alembic migrations plus focused unit, contract, API, and real-PostgreSQL
  verification;
- model-owned coordination strategy inside state-specific tool grants, with no
  deterministic coordinator invoked after model or sandbox failure;
- a durable run created before inference, exact terminal retry without a second
  model call, and restart recovery fenced by the same lease that bounds tool
  authority;
- a fixed-argv one-run sandbox worker that uses LangChain Deep Agents with a
  tool-capable vLLM endpoint through either the explicitly selected NemoClaw
  managed route or the content-locked Docker gateway graph;
- one private capability-authenticated tool POST path with fresh scope, state,
  policy, schema, audit, and idempotency enforcement;
- a bounded private tool executor isolated from long-lived API workers, plus an
  absolute NemoClaw launcher that receives no backend configuration secrets;
- host-reconciled body-free tool evidence and a reviewed host-rendered terminal
  summary instead of persisted model prose; and
- immutable ACE playbook/context contracts that admit only reviewed host
  templates and safe provenance partitions; and
- offline candidate evolution that can propose and evaluate policy changes but
  cannot self-authorize production activation.

